(158768, 3190, 87, 'I''m really happy that you''re doing this research, but I struggled with a few of the questions.  In my experience, I''ve seen people be very open about more common disorders, like anxiety and depression.  I''ve struggled with both at different points throughout my life, and it didn''t seem like that big of a deal.  However, I''ve met a number of people in tech who deal with more complex and challenging issues, like bipolar disorder, which seems like a completely different thing to me, both in how it affects the person who has it, and how society reacts to it.  It''s hard to clump them all together.', 'I''m really happy that you''re doing this research, but I struggled with a few of the questions.  In my experience, I''ve seen people be very open about more common disorders, like anxiety and depression.  I''ve struggled with both at different points throughout my life, and it didn''t seem like that big of a deal.  However, I''ve met a number of people in tech who deal with more complex and challenging issues, like bipolar disorder, which seems like a completely different thing to me, both in how it affects the person who has it, and how society reacts to it.  It''s hard to clump them all together.'),
