(161199, 3222, 86, 'Stop advocating late-hour work and meeting impossible deadlines as the cool thing to do. Openly admit to feelings of anxiety or frustration or depression, especially from people in leading roles. Look for ways to maximise "effective work" rather than "8 hours a day". Allow (and applaud) taking a break if things are not working. Allow (and applaud) taking care of not work-related issues if they are worrying.', 'Stop advocating late-hour work and meeting impossible deadlines as the cool thing to do. Openly admit to feelings of anxiety or frustration or depression, especially from people in leading roles. Look for ways to maximise "effective work" rather than "8 hours a day". Allow (and applaud) taking a break if things are not working. Allow (and applaud) taking care of not work-related issues if they are worrying.'),
