(168723, 3321, 86, 'The majority of the tech industry only pays lip service to true work/life balance. They talk about how important work/life balance is but they only truly reward the workaholics resulting in the crazy 50-60 hour work weeks and crunch time stories we all hear about and experience. Tech companies are designed as engines to turn youthful ambition into money in the most efficient way possible ... by burning through people and only keeping the absolute strongest, luckiest, or most ruthless.', 'The majority of the tech industry only pays lip service to true work/life balance. They talk about how important work/life balance is but they only truly reward the workaholics resulting in the crazy 50-60 hour work weeks and crunch time stories we all hear about and experience. Tech companies are designed as engines to turn youthful ambition into money in the most efficient way possible ... by burning through people and only keeping the absolute strongest, luckiest, or most ruthless.'),
