(185899, 3547, 86, 'Employers of small- and medium-size companies don''t pay ANY attention to employee''s health. The only thing that matters is making the money.', 'Employers of small- and medium-size companies don''t pay ANY attention to employee''s health. The only thing that matters is making the money.'),
(185900, 3547, 87, 'Yes, the first question "self-employed" should be precised. I am self-employed but working for a bigger company (my only client) - this is most popular business model in Poland but self-employed employees are treated as regular employees, without any differences. It''s just for tax purposes - as I said, small- and medium-size businesses care only about money, so they eagerly hire self-employed people to optimize their costs and taxes, obviously (without any responsibility on the employer side that other hiring options have). I just don''t want this questionnaire to be interpreted in wrong way.', 'Yes, the first question "self-employed" should be precised. I am self-employed but working for a bigger company (my only client) - this is most popular business model in Poland but self-employed employees are treated as regular employees, without any differences. It''s just for tax purposes - as I said, small- and medium-size businesses care only about money, so they eagerly hire self-employed people to optimize their costs and taxes, obviously (without any responsibility on the employer side that other hiring options have). I just don''t want this questionnaire to be interpreted in wrong way.'),
