(195855, 3678, 86, 'Stop lionizing and promoting manic episodes as normal or desirable methods of producing work. The culture doesn''t allow for enough self-care — when you have to work 12+ hour days, then respond outside office hours to emails/IMs, it''s difficult to build in enough time to sleep enough, or take breaks for meals, or exercise, or meditate. The glorification of people who spend their entire lives working in a frenzied trance state is extremely difficult to live up to, and a potential trigger for mania. ', 'Stop lionizing and promoting manic episodes as normal or desirable methods of producing work. The culture doesn''t allow for enough self-care — when you have to work 12+ hour days, then respond outside office hours to emails/IMs, it''s difficult to build in enough time to sleep enough, or take breaks for meals, or exercise, or meditate. The glorification of people who spend their entire lives working in a frenzied trance state is extremely difficult to live up to, and a potential trigger for mania.'),
