(203531, 3779, 86, 'Hard-stop on the long-hours bragging.  A company where people routinely work longer than 40 hours a week should be one with no employees, and employers should be ashamed to admit that they do that.  Job ads for "we work so hard all the time all day and all night" are a sign of company sickness.', 'Hard-stop on the long-hours bragging.  A company where people routinely work longer than 40 hours a week should be one with no employees, and employers should be ashamed to admit that they do that.  Job ads for "we work so hard all the time all day and all night" are a sign of company sickness.'),
