(221984, 4022, 71, 'I''ve had to take time off for mental health (usually about 4 weeks) a few times in my career. I usually have to hit the breaking point before changes are made to my workload or anxiety-producing situation. I have also resigned due to mental health (and in one case, returned later).', 'I''ve had to take time off for mental health (usually about 4 weeks) a few times in my career. I usually have to hit the breaking point before changes are made to my workload or anxiety-producing situation. I have also resigned due to mental health (and in one case, returned later).'),
(221985, 4022, 72, '1', '1'),
(221986, 4022, 73, 'Mostly supportive. People either reveal their own mental health struggles (surprisingly common) or try to understand. Sometimes I end up feeling worse if I can tell they are struggling themselves but act like they''ve got it all together and seem determined not to show weakness. I''ve also occasionally had people become very uncomfortable and then withdraw from the relationship.', 'Mostly supportive. People either reveal their own mental health struggles (surprisingly common) or try to understand. Sometimes I end up feeling worse if I can tell they are struggling themselves but act like they''ve got it all together and seem determined not to show weakness. I''ve also occasionally had people become very uncomfortable and then withdraw from the relationship.'),
(221987, 4022, 74, '1', '1'),
(221988, 4022, 75, 'One manager told me about her bipolar disorder. She was a huge support to me at the time.', 'One manager told me about her bipolar disorder. She was a huge support to me at the time.'),
