(19448, 748, 103, 'Italians are somewhat behind for what concerns mental health care in the workplace.  Physical health care is very much accepted with a doctor that certifies your ailment.  Mental health is treated quite differently, I believe, because most people are willing to admit that physical ailments should be covered while mental ailments are almost considered non-existent in most respects.  ', 'Italians are somewhat behind for what concerns mental health care in the workplace.  Physical health care is very much accepted with a doctor that certifies your ailment.  Mental health is treated quite differently, I believe, because most people are willing to admit that physical ailments should be covered while mental ailments are almost considered non-existent in most respects.'),
