(171611, 3359, 86, 'I think we should all talk more openly about mental health.  That also requires that we have empathy for those that do talk about it.', 'I think we should all talk more openly about mental health.  That also requires that we have empathy for those that do talk about it.'),
(171612, 3359, 87, 'I feel the IT industry gets labeled as a ''low stress'' career.  At the end of the day our bodies my not feel the same as a brick layer but our minds have been through the ringer.  We are constantly working through problems and rarely do we disconnect entirely when we leave the office.  You are only laying bricks while you are at work but for IT we can be ''working'' around the clock.  That stress adds up and isn''t always easy to understand as the person going through it, or easy to identify as a person seeing it happen.', 'I feel the IT industry gets labeled as a ''low stress'' career.  At the end of the day our bodies my not feel the same as a brick layer but our minds have been through the ringer.  We are constantly working through problems and rarely do we disconnect entirely when we leave the office.  You are only laying bricks while you are at work but for IT we can be ''working'' around the clock.  That stress adds up and isn''t always easy to understand as the person going through it, or easy to identify as a person seeing it happen.'),
