(206267, 3815, 86, 'Actively work against the culture of over-doing it (late hours, caffeinate to keep going, etc.).  Encourage people to work on open source projects on company time so that they don''t need do so on their own time.  No "crunch time" should ever last more than a week; if it does, it means management screwed up and it''s their problem, not the developers''.', 'Actively work against the culture of over-doing it (late hours, caffeinate to keep going, etc.).  Encourage people to work on open source projects on company time so that they don''t need do so on their own time.  No "crunch time" should ever last more than a week; if it does, it means management screwed up and it''s their problem, not the developers''.'),
