(214930, 3929, 85, '4', '4'),
(214931, 3929, 86, 'There''s the obvious answer of adding mental health coverage to insurance plans, regular talks/presentations about mental health and preservation, and cultivating a more supportive environment surrounding it. But there really isn''t a way to remove the stigma. Because no matter how supportive a company is in their programs or message, employers and hiring managers will always have an implicit doubt on an employee/potential hire''s ability, work ethic, and reliability if they ever reveal they have a mental health issue.', 'There''s the obvious answer of adding mental health coverage to insurance plans, regular talks/presentations about mental health and preservation, and cultivating a more supportive environment surrounding it. But there really isn''t a way to remove the stigma. Because no matter how supportive a company is in their programs or message, employers and hiring managers will always have an implicit doubt on an employee/potential hire''s ability, work ethic, and reliability if they ever reveal they have a mental health issue.'),
